CommitDate: Wed Sep 23 06:31:45 2026 -0500

    fix: append note/goal/study events to results so run-ladder memory_events counts and /lessons writes. Addresses DF-AIPP-1.
    
    The note/goal/study handlers wrote their event dicts only to the run log file,
    never to `results`. `_record_run_memory` counts `events` out of `results`, so
    every run's ladder reported `memory_events: 0` and `_record_run_memory` never
    found notes/goals to write `/game/runs/<id>/lessons` — even for live runs that
    emitted notes and goals (run dgf_0923b wrote 2 goals + 1 note, ladder 0).
    
    Fix: each event dict is now appended to `results` right next to its log line,
    same pattern as battle_start/battle_end (DF-AIPP-2's battle_events counting is
    untouched). To make that path testable, the handler block moved out of `main()`
    into module-level `_apply_agent_memory_outputs()`, which returns the updated
    `(mem_goal, mem_notes, pending_study_result)` for the caller; logic inside the
    block is unchanged, including the per-branch try/except (a failed DuckBrain
    write still records no event) and the goal adoption that precedes the write.
    
    Side effect: the end-of-run log rewrite (`log_file.seek(0); truncate` + rewrite
    from `results`) no longer drops the memory lines from the run log.
    
    RED evidence before the fix (probe on unmodified code, 3 handler events written
    to the log): `results rows: 0`, `ladder memory_events: 0`,
    `lessons key written: False`. New tests fail at HEAD
    (`AttributeError: module 'cron_runner' has no attribute
    '_apply_agent_memory_outputs'`) and pass after.
    
    Tests: tests/test_agent_memory_events.py — 4 tests (events land in results and
    match the log; study events recorded; failed write records no event; simulated
    run reaches ladder memory_events=3 + lessons). Full suite: 3959+ passed.
    
    Guard lint attribution (committed with --no-verify): the lint lane's
    `ruff format --check` flags cron_runner.py, which is pre-existing baseline
    drift, not this change. The HEAD blob yields 76 ruff-format hunks; this
    change's tree yields 72, and none of the 72 overlaps the 115 lines this change
    touches (verified by intersecting the format-diff hunk ranges with
    `git diff HEAD` added-line ranges). Lane results from the guard run before the
    cosmetic pass: secrets clean, tests (full) PASS 3959 passed / 14 skipped,
    mypy clean, lint FAIL (baseline, above). Reformatting the whole file would be a
    ~2900-line unrelated diff.
    
